@startuml architecture-mushroom-mood
title Mushroom Mood Current-State Architecture Flow

' Status: Implemented
' Purpose: Show the current implemented boundaries for the Mushroom Mood readiness flow after observation-backed seasonality was added.

actor User
participant "Mushroom Mood UI" as AppUi
participant "Mushroom Readiness API Route" as ReadinessRoute
participant "Readiness Service" as ReadinessService
database "Curated Species Catalog and Rules" as SpeciesCatalog
participant "Weather History Service" as WeatherHistoryService
participant "Weather Data Repository" as WeatherDataRepository
participant "Seasonal Observation Repository" as SeasonalObservationRepository
database "In-Memory Seasonal Evidence Cache" as SeasonalEvidenceCache
participant "SMHI API" as SmhiApi
participant "ArtDatabanken Observation Search API" as ObservationSearchApi

User -> AppUi: Choose spot and species
AppUi -> ReadinessRoute: Request readiness, confidence, and explanation data
ReadinessRoute -> ReadinessService: Build result for selected spot and species
ReadinessService -> SpeciesCatalog: Load curated species metadata and seasonal rules
ReadinessService -> WeatherHistoryService: Load recent weather evidence for the spot
WeatherHistoryService -> WeatherDataRepository: Select stations and request measurements
WeatherDataRepository -> SmhiApi: Fetch station catalog and weather history data
SmhiApi --> WeatherDataRepository: Weather history data
WeatherDataRepository --> WeatherHistoryService: Station measurements
WeatherHistoryService --> ReadinessService: Rainfall and temperature history
ReadinessService -> SeasonalObservationRepository: Load seasonal observation evidence for the spot and species
SeasonalObservationRepository -> SeasonalEvidenceCache: Read processed seasonal evidence

alt Fresh seasonal evidence is cached
  SeasonalEvidenceCache --> SeasonalObservationRepository: Fresh processed seasonal evidence
else Cache is missing or expired
  SeasonalObservationRepository -> ObservationSearchApi: Search observations by stored taxon ID, spot, radius, and lookback policy
  ObservationSearchApi --> SeasonalObservationRepository: Observation records
  SeasonalObservationRepository -> SeasonalEvidenceCache: Store processed seasonal evidence in memory
  SeasonalEvidenceCache --> SeasonalObservationRepository: Cached processed seasonal evidence
else Live refresh fails but stale cache is reusable
  SeasonalEvidenceCache --> SeasonalObservationRepository: Stale processed seasonal evidence with freshness limitation
end

SeasonalObservationRepository --> ReadinessService: Seasonal evidence summary

alt Required inputs are available
  ReadinessService -> ReadinessService: Use observation-backed seasonality when evidence is sufficient
  ReadinessService -> SpeciesCatalog: Fall back to static seasonal timing when observation evidence is sparse or missing
  ReadinessService -> ReadinessService: Combine seasonal evidence, weather, and species thresholds
  ReadinessService --> ReadinessRoute: Readiness label, probability, confidence, and explanation inputs
  ReadinessRoute --> AppUi: 200 OK result payload
  AppUi --> User: Show result, confidence, limitations, and seasonal evidence details
else Inputs are partial or missing
  ReadinessService --> ReadinessRoute: Low-confidence or unavailable result with missing-data reasons
  ReadinessRoute --> AppUi: Result payload with limitations
  AppUi --> User: Show low-confidence or unavailable state
end

note right of ReadinessService
Observation-backed seasonality is the primary path.
If evidence is sparse or missing, the service falls back
to static season months in the curated species catalog
and lowers confidence.
The readiness response exposes grouped seasonal evidence
details for transparency in the UI.
end note

note right of SeasonalEvidenceCache
Current implementation uses an in-memory cache for
processed seasonal evidence.
The long-run target remains a persistent derived-evidence cache.
end note

@enduml